      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T14:03:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This rule (no `%` primitives and no `Native` links outside Vali\u0027s own libraries) covers the `invoke` section only. A procedure transformer\u0027s IR in the syntax export goes straight to `converted` (transformers.rs) and loads into the phase isolate unchecked. So any library\u0027s macro can link any `%` primitive, or any registered native library, at expansion time. The same check should run on transformer IR, allowing what `syntax-case` itself links: `%syntax-match`, `%syntax-build` and `%quote-syntax`.",
      "revId": "060ee05cbaf46b808397560b4cf19185d2be80b2",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
